Pseudonymization and Tokenization of Identifiers
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Load and manage sensitive identifier data (Emirates IDs) in PostgreSQL
Implement format-preserving tokenization using Python
Separate token vaults from operational data with restrictive file/database permissions
Perform controlled reidentification through an authorized access path
Document residual risk and key management controls aligned with GDPR Art. 32 and GCC PDPL
Prerequisites
Basic SQL (INSERT, SELECT, GRANT/REVOKE)
Basic Python (functions, dictionaries, file I/O)
Familiarity with Linux file permissions (chmod, chown)
Understanding of pseudonymization vs. anonymization concepts
Environment Setup
Your Al Nafi Linux machine comes with a terminal. Install required packages:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y postgresql postgresql-contrib python3-pip
sudo systemctl start postgresql
sudo systemctl enable postgresql
pip3 install psycopg2-binary cryptography
Create a database and working user:

sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE DATABASE privacy_lab;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE USER lab_app WITH PASSWORD 'LabPass123';"
sudo -u postgres psql -d privacy_lab -c "GRANT CONNECT ON DATABASE privacy_lab TO lab_app;"
Task 1: Load Sample Dataset with Emirates IDs
